# Seven Segment Display Using 8051

## Project Description
This project focuses on interfacing a seven-segment display with the 8051 microcontroller to represent numerical data through electronic signals.

## Project Objectives
- Understand 8051 microcontroller architecture.
- Learn seven-segment display interfacing.
- Develop basic embedded C programming skills.
- Understand digital output control.

## Hardware Requirements
- 8051 Microcontroller
- Seven Segment Display
- Current-Limiting Resistors
- Breadboard and Jumper Wires
- DC Power Supply

## Software Requirements
- Embedded C Compiler
- 8051 Simulator (optional)

## Expected Result
The seven-segment display shows the intended numerical digits according to the programmed output signals.

## Conclusion
This project provides practical experience in microcontroller interfacing and embedded systems development.
